    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a really helpful perspective for the character. Some of the historians I've been reading suggest that officials in your position didn't just see it as a matter of governance, but actually believed there were inherent, biological differences in intelligence or character between the British and the Indians. In your character's view, would you say they are fundamentally different types of people, or is it just a matter of culture?",
